On Nov 20, 2008, at 3:35 PM, Ben Bolker wrote:

> I can never remember exactly which address is subscribed to the list.


You shouldn't need to worry about this, or at least not if the mailing  
list is set up correctly. What we normally do is hold postings from  
non-members (rather than discard them), and when releasing them (if  
they are legitimate) also whitelist the sender address (the admin  
interface lets you do this in the same swoop). That way your other  
addresses will be held only once.

Of course, that system is easily defeated by people who immediately  
withdraw their held posting and then scramble to figure out which  
address they should be sending from :-)

